# Repository-wide: store text as LF and check it out as LF on every platform,
# so that a Windows clone and a Linux clone are byte-identical. The
# reproducible-build claim is verified on x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, so this is
# load-bearing rather than cosmetic.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Conformance fixtures are byte-exact inputs vendored from JSONTestSuite.
# 25 of them are not valid UTF-8, several contain NUL bytes, and two are
# 100 000 levels deep: the exact bytes ARE the test. Git must never convert
# them, on commit, on clone, or on a CI runner.
#
# The same rule covers real_world/, which is not vendored: four of those
# documents were written by PowerShell with CRLF line endings, and converting
# them would change what the round-trip test measures.
tests/fixtures/** -text

# All of it is data rather than code, so it is kept out of the language
# statistics. The upstream commit and licence for the vendored half are in
# ATTRIBUTION.md; real_world/PROVENANCE.md covers the other half.
tests/fixtures/** linguist-vendored